ed, truncated, and missing-final-newline JSONL; recursive forgeries, orphan/partial/reversed/duplicate/replayed/conflicting calls, wrong accepted text/details, and post-result rows; valid Coder, Fixer, Judge, Reviewer, and Collector native lifecycles including Collector projection and Judge/Reviewer usage; derivative scan truth; child exit/signal versus v2 sealer failure; admission-before-spawn; no-replace publication races; and raw sessions absent from dockets.\n\nAt the real production stream-forwarding seam, feed the same reusable buffer enough times to represent more than 2 GiB into a counting/discard writable—without a 2 GiB file or aggregate Buffer—and assert exact logical byte count, bounded ring capacity, backpressure completion, and unchanged sealing inputs. Add a modest spawned-child integration proving irrelevant stdout pass-through. Finish with recorder build, typecheck, full tests, package inventory, and clean installed-bin invocation.\n\n## C9 — Scope\nPreserve caller-owned role order, repetition, routing, and workflow topology. Add no model selection, scheduler, retries, rounds, automatic Git mutation, raw-session archive, second storage temperature, or retention daemon. Do not implement #12 Doctor/StatsLine, #13 retry/recurrence, #22, or the broad #26 sweep. Do not change bundled Souls merely because transport/schema changed; schema, runtime, and README own these mechanical laws. Prefer deletion and seam replacement over compatibility adapters."
